+{"id": "c3849e1033a8", "title": "Consolidate flask-restx model registration and extract URL validators", "description": "Two related quality issues in the API layer:\n\n### 1. Triple-registered models\n`add_models_to_api` in `app/models.py` builds and returns a fresh dict of models every time it is called. It is currently called THREE times: once from `app/__init__.py` on the top-level `Api`, once from `app/api/endpoints.py` on its `Namespace`, once from `app/api/settings.py` on its `Namespace`. Each call registers a new model instance \u2014 the objects that `endpoints.py:models[\"endpoint\"]` and `__init__.py`s api models refer to are DIFFERENT objects. flask-restx tolerates this but it wastes work and makes the intent unclear.\n\n### 2. URL validation lives in the API layer\n`normalize_url` and `validate_url` are defined at the top of `app/api/endpoints.py`. They have no HTTP or Flask dependency and belong in a domain module so tests and future callers (e.g., a CLI) can reuse them.\n\n## What to change\n1. Refactor `app/models.py`:\n   - Split `add_models_to_api` into two functions:\n     - `build_models(api_or_ns)` \u2014 the existing body, unchanged (some flask-restx workflows need per-namespace registration for swagger discoverability, so preserve it as-is).\n     - Add a module-level cache: `_MODELS: dict | None = None` and `def get_models(api) -> dict:` that lazily calls `build_models(api)` ONCE and returns the cached dict on subsequent calls.\n   - Keep `add_models_to_api` as a thin alias for `build_models` for backwards compat with the two namespace files during migration.\n2. Update `app/api/endpoints.py`:\n   - Move `normalize_url` and `validate_url` (plus the inner `is_valid_ipv4`) to NEW file `app/core/validators.py`.\n   - Import them: `from ..core.validators import normalize_url, validate_url`.\n   - No behavior change; identical function bodies.\n3. Update `app/api/settings.py`: no logic change needed unless it breaks \u2014 leave as-is (keeps its `add_models_to_api(ns)` call for now).\n4. Create `app/core/validators.py` with the two functions (plus the inner helper made module-private as `_is_valid_ipv4`).\n\n## Files you own\n`app/models.py`, `app/api/endpoints.py`, `app/api/settings.py`, and NEW file `app/core/validators.py`. Nothing else. In particular, do NOT touch `app/__init__.py` (Task 5 owns it), `app/core/monitoring.py` (Task 3), `app/core/telegram_bot.py` (Task 4), `app/repositories/*` (Task 2), or `app/core/startup.py` (Task 5).\n\n## Acceptance\n- `app/core/validators.py` exists and exports `normalize_url`, `validate_url`.\n- `grep -n \"def normalize_url\" app/api/endpoints.py` returns nothing.\n- `grep -n \"def validate_url\" app/api/endpoints.py` returns nothing.\n- `grep -n \"def get_models\" app/models.py` returns 1 match.\n- `python -c \"from app.core.validators import normalize_url, validate_url; assert validate_url(\\\"example.com\\\"); assert not validate_url(\\\"not a url with spaces\\\"); print(normalize_url(\\\"example.com\\\"))\"` prints `https://example.com` and exits 0.", "role": "architect", "priority": 2, "scope": "medium", "complexity": "medium", "estimated_minutes": 120, "status": "done", "task_type": "standard", "upgrade_details": null, "depends_on": [], "parent_task_id": null, "depends_on_repo": null, "owned_files": ["app/models.py", "app/api/endpoints.py", "app/api/settings.py", "app/core/validators.py"], "assigned_agent": null, "result_summary": "Split app/models.py::add_models_to_api into build_models (per-namespace body preserved) + cached get_models(api); kept add_models_to_api as thin alias for backward compat. Extracted normalize_url and validate_url (with inner _is_valid_ipv4) from app/api/endpoints.py into new app/core/validators.py \u2014 identical bodies, no behavior change. endpoints.py now imports them from ..core.validators. All acceptance checks pass (validators file exists, no def normalize_url/validate_url left in endpoints.py, def get_models present in models